2026-07-27T15:05:59.5863549Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5863954Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5864325Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5864712Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5865071Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5865430Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5865797Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5866172Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5866549Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5866864Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5867119Z [36;1mempty_makevars="$(mktemp)"[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5867375Z [36;1mfor var in CC CXX CXX11 CXX14 CXX17 CXX20 CXX23; do[0m
2026-07-27T15:05:59.5867734Z [36;1m  val="$(R_MAKEVARS_USER="$empty_makevars" R CMD config "$var" 2>/dev/null || true)"[0m
